      "title": "Head Cheerleading Coach",
      "description": "Head Cheerleading Coach | Greensboro College Skip to content About GC Alumni Give To GC Translate Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Greensboro College Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Search Menu Home » Employment » Head Cheerleading Coach Head Cheerleading Coach Head Cheerleading Coach Full-Time JOB SUMMARY: Greensboro College, an NCAA Division III institution located in Greensboro, North Carolina, is accepting applications from qualified candidates for the role of Head Coach of the Cheer program. This position is responsible for recruiting and building a roster as we reinstate the Cheer program with the anticipation of game/competition cheer beginning in the fall of 2027. The head coach’s roles and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following: Recruit talented student-athletes and build a roster to compete beginning in the Fall of 2027. Consistently communicate recruiting strategies and numbers to the Director of Athletics Develop and implement training plans focused on skill development, safety, and performance. Lead practices, choreography sessions, and game-day performances Maintain a safe training environment and enforce risk-management protocols Mentor student-athletes in academic progress, personal conduct, and leadership Promote a positive, inclusive, and team-oriented culture Maintain accurate recruitment records and communication logs Prepare cheer team for campus and community appearances Manage program budget, purchasing, and financial procedures in accordance with College policies to ensure stewardship of resources Coordinate travel arrangements, itineraries, and event logistics, transporting student-athletes as needed Supervise assistant coaches, volunteers, and student workers Ensure adherence to Greensboro College, conference, and national governing-body regulations Fully participate in department meetings, campus events, and community outreach Collaborate with athletics staff and campus partners to support program operations Submits requested departmental forms in a timely manner Develop fundraising strategies to enhance the overall student-athlete experience Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics QUALIFICATIONS: Required Bachelor’s degree Prior coaching experience in cheer, dance, or a related discipline Knowledge of safety standards based upon NCAA guidelines CPR/First Aid certification or ability to obtain upon Preferred Collegiate-level coaching experience Experience supervising staff or student workers About Greensboro College: Greensboro College Athletics sponsors 20 NCAA sports and two more club sports. Recognized nationally and a member of the USA South (primary) and Old Dominion Athletic Conference (affiliate). Founded in 1838, Greensboro College empowers students to define their individual paths toward a life of fulfillment, achievement, and impact. After more than 186 years, we’re still finding new ways to grow stronger and help students do the same. Located in Greensboro, North Carolina, Greensboro College is education made personal. With a 10:1 student-faculty ratio and excellent student support services, students receive the personal attention and guidance they need to thrive in the classroom and beyond. GC offers big-city connections. Just steps from campus, there are internship and job opportunities, great shopping, restaurants, and the hopping nightlife of downtown Greensboro. We pride ourselves on being where affordable meets exceptional. Greensboro College makes an extraordinary education affordable as one of the least expensive private schools in North Carolina. Link to Apply: https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/D02D24249A4B0AC5D0B14E565B814B72/jobs/521741 Create Your Path of Discovery Today Apply Visit Request Info 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 336.272.7102 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Campus Conduct Hotline Con