    "https://www.greensboro.edu/academics/student-success/career-personal-development/": {
      "title": "Career & Personal Development",
      "description": "Career & Personal Development | Greensboro College Skip to content About GC Alumni Give To GC Translate Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Greensboro College Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Search Menu Home » Academics » Student Success » Career & Personal Development Career & Personal Development Career & Personal Development Online Career Guide What Can I Do With This Major? LinkedIn Learning Internships Resumes For Employers Grow into a great career and fulfilling life The Office of Career and Personal Development supports the personal, educational, and professional growth of students and alumni, helping them develop the skills to make a positive impact wherever they live and work. With our guidance, Greensboro College students develop greater self-awareness, allowing them to identify their strengths, personal values, and interests as they chart their path to a bright future. As the pursuit of a successful career is an ongoing journey, our office is dedicated to fostering the continuous growth and employability of Greensboro College students from enrollment through graduation and throughout their entire professional lives. Career and Personal Development assists students and alumni with: Exploring career options within majors Cultivating networking, job search, and interpersonal competencies to enhance employability in an ever-evolving professional landscape Gaining hands-on experience through career shadowing, internships, and relevant work experience Assistance with applying to graduate or professional school Prepare to follow your dreams Hear from Greensboro College student Liya Veale, intern at the Kellin Foundation, a non-profit dedicated to strengthening resilience among children, families, adults and communities through trauma-informed behavioral health services focused on prevention, treatment, and healing. greensboro college online career development guide This detailed Online Career Development Guide helps Greensboro College students embark on their career planning path, outlining clear steps from their first year through graduation. The guide is divided into the following sections to allow for ease of searching content: Self-Awareness Explore Options Build Experience & Skills Create Your Professional Materials Apply, Interview, & Decide Transition After Graduation Email questions to: caryn.atwater@greensboro.edu . Contact Us Caryn J Atwater, M.A. Director, Career and Personal Development Greensboro College, Room 321 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 Phone: (336) 272-7102 x5370 Send Email Find Greensboro College on Instagram @greensborocollegecareers Follow on Instagram Create Your Path of Discovery Today Apply Visit Request Info 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 336.272.7102 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Campus Conduct Hotline Conferences & Events Contact Us Employment Pride Page IT Resources Faculty / Staff Intranet Library Moodle Pride Shop Online Store Privacy Policy Registrar / Request Transcript Safety and Security See All Events Sexual Harassment Sitemap Student Sharepoint If you have difficulty accessing information on the site due to a disability or other issues, please contact: webmaster@greensboro.edu Copyright © 2026 Greensboro College | All rights reserved. Close Menu Close Menu Academics Undergraduate Degree Requirements Full Course Catalog School of the Arts Department of Theatre Audition Information Theatre Facilities Past Productions Theatre Scholarships Department of Music Ensembles Department of Art Performance Calendar School of Business Department of Business Administration & Economics Department of Accounting School of Humanities Department of English, Communication & Media Studies Department of History Department of Religion, Ethics & Philosophy School of Sciences & Mathematics Department of Kinesiology Department of Mathematics Department of Natural Sciences 