rary Borrowing Databases Collection Development Plan Course Guides e-textbooks Levy-Loewenstein Holocaust Collection Library Policies Visit the Campus Campus Map Give To GC Endowments Give4GC Honor Roll of Donors Peter Doub Society Pride Club Development Staff Alumni Alumni Awards Alumni Board Alumni Notes ALUMNI EVENTS Alumni Spotlight Recent Graduates Alumni Contact Update Form Donate your Time and Talent Alumni Awards Alumni Award Nomination Form Alumni Notes Alumni Notes Form Current Students Residence Life Health Services Public Safety & Security Student Life Student Success Student Handbook Health Services Covid-19 Resources Immunizations & Vaccinations Counseling Services Health Privacy Notice Public Safety & Security Campus Conduct Hotline Sexual Harassment Sexual Harassment Report Sexual Harassment Faculty & Staff Resources Faculty Directory Faculty / Staff Intranet Center for the Enhancement of Teaching and Learning Parents Your Student’s Pride Card Events Performance Calendar Event Reservations/Rentals TALGS Conference Search “I loved the GC Honors program and Greensboro College. I felt safe and a sense of genuine belonging at the college. I worked closely with my thesis advisor and professors who helped inspire me to define my path and passion of interest. That path has led me to complete my doctoral studies in Engineering Mechanics.” - Dr. Josh Fitzgerald, Class of ’19, Mathematics Major Dr. Josh Fitzgerald earned his master's from Virginia Tech University (studied astrodynamics) as well as earning an Engineering Mechanics Ph.D. He joined the NASA Johnson Space Center in Houston, TX as an Advanced Mission Design Engineer, optimizing trajectories for the Artemis II and III missions to return humans to the moon. Visit Apply Request Info Search Search Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility"
