    "https://www.greensboro.edu/academics/student-success/career-personal-development/employers/": {
      "title": "Graduate School & Certifications",
      "description": "For Employers | Greensboro College Skip to content About GC Alumni Give To GC Translate Arabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Greensboro College Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student Life Athletics Search Menu Home » Academics » Student Success » Career & Personal Development » For Employers Graduate School & Certifications Career & Personal Development Online Career Guide What Can I Do With This Major? LinkedIn Learning Internships Resumes For Employers LinkedIn Lunch Time Career Connections Complete this form to request a day to participate in our Lunch Time Career Connections program Lunch Time Career Connections allow employers and graduate and professional schools the opportunity to speak to Greensboro College students about their organization, available internship and employment opportunities, and programs while mingling with students outside the Fowler Dining Hall during the lunch hours, a less formal environment. Format Lunch Time Career Connections can happen on most any day of your choosing. A table is set up outside the student dining area between the hours of 11:00 and 1:30, the heaviest traffic hours. Enjoy meeting our students while raising awareness of your organization. Don’t forget to bring materials that will help our students learn about your organization and potential opportunities! Employers and professionals who wish to come to campus to meet Greensboro College students and talk to them about their organization, internship and employment opportunities should complete the form linked at the top of this page. You may also email us at caryn.atwater@greensboro.edu for further information. Lunch Time Career Connections are also a great opportunity for GC alum to give back to Greensboro College and current students by coming back and speaking to our students about topics and issues that will help them to be successful. Offer Internship Opportunities Internships help students gain valuable work experience, define interests, sharpen skills, evaluate plans for employment or graduate studies and make professional connections. Benefits to the Employer: Gain input and fresh perspective from enthusiastic and motivated students Enlist interns to complete special projects Each semester hour credit requires 45 clock hours of work. Typically, students receive 4 credits requiring an average of 12 clock hours per week, a total of 180 clock hours for the semester (based on a 15 week semester) For more information on Greensboro College Internships, visit our internship page or contact Caryn J Atwater, Director of Career and Personal Development, at caryn.atwater@greensboro.edu. Interested in Posting an Opportunity with Greensboro College? Employers and organizations wishing to share opportunities with Greensboro College may send the Director of Career and Personal Development any relevant information, which will then be shared with all students, faculty and staff.  The following information is helpful when sending a posting: Position title Days, times, hours/wk, duration of assignment Location Contact person, phone and/or email address Responsibilities Qualifications required Volunteer, internship (paid or unpaid), part-time, or full-time Salary Other requirements such as reliable transportation Certifications Please send your information to Caryn J Atwater at caryn.atwater@greensboro.edu . Create Your Path of Discovery Today Apply Visit Request Info 815 W. Market Street Greensboro, NC 27401 336.272.7102 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Campus Conduct Hotline Conferences & Events Contact Us Employment Pride Page IT Resources Faculty / Staff Intranet Library Moodle Pride Shop Online Store Privacy Policy Registrar / Request Transcript Safety and Security See All Events Sexual Harassment Sitemap Student Sharepoint If you have difficulty accessing information on the site due to a disability or other issues, please contact: webmaster@greensboro.edu Copyright © 2026 Greensboro College | All rights reserved. Close Menu Close Menu Academics Undergraduate Degree Requirements Full Course Catalog School of the Arts Department of Theatre Audition Information Theatre Facilities Past Productions Theatre Scholarships Department of Music Ensembles Department of Art Performance Calendar School of Business Department of Business Administration & Economics Department of Accounting School of Humanities Department of English, Communication & Media Studies Department of History Department of Religion, Ethics & Philosophy School of Sciences & Mathematics Department of Kinesiology Department of Mathematics Department of Natural Sciences School of Social Sciences & Education Department of Education Department of Political Science & Global Affairs Department of Psychology Department of Sociology & Criminal Justice Graduate Programs Educator Preparation Program Professional Development International Programs & Study Abroad Student Academic Achievements Honors Program Student Success Your Path Forward Accessibility Support Accommodation Request Form PEAK Team Career & Personal Development Explore Your Interests, Personality and Strengths Explore Majors & Research Careers Internships Resumes, Cover Letters & More Job Search, Salaries, Offers, & Negotiation Graduate School For Employers Office of Student Success Global Communication Center Peer Tutoring, Supplemental Instruction Program, and Math Support Universal Design for Learning Registrar Transcript Requests Transfer Policy Records & Privacy Policy Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Fees International Student Tuition Payments Accepted Students High School Students Graduate and Licensure Students 23 and Older Undergraduate Students Transfer Students International Students First-Year & Transfer Student Checklist Request Information Admissions FAQ Admissions Team Financial Aid Outside Scholarships Types of Aid Available Apply for Financial Aid Payment Options View and Accept Fin